āsuraṁ pārtha me śṛṇu\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":4163,\"bb\":3662,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/16/6/b3662/\",\"shadow_value\":\"dvau – two; bhūta-sargau – created living beings; loke – in the world; asmin – this; daivaḥ – godly; āsuraḥ – demoniac; eva – certainly; ca – and; daivaḥ – the divine; vistaraśaḥ – at great length; proktaḥ – said; āsuram – the demoniac; pārtha – O son of Pṛthā; me – from Me; śṛṇu – just hear.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"dvau\",\"translation\":\"two\"},{\"word\":\"bhūta-sargau\",\"translation\":\"created living beings\"},{\"word\":\"loke\",\"translation\":\"in the world\"},{\"word\":\"asmin\",\"translation\":\"this\"},{\"word\":\"daivaḥ\",\"translation\":\"godly\"},{\"word\":\"āsuraḥ\",\"translation\":\"demoniac\"},{\"word\":\"eva\",\"translation\":\"certainly\"},{\"word\":\"ca\",\"translation\":\"and\"},{\"word\":\"daivaḥ\",\"translation\":\"the divine\"},{\"word\":\"vistaraśaḥ\",\"translation\":\"at great length\"},{\"word\":\"proktaḥ\",\"translation\":\"said\"},{\"word\":\"āsuram\",\"translation\":\"the demoniac\"},{\"word\":\"pārtha\",\"translation\":\"O son of Pṛthā\"},{\"word\":\"me\",\"translation\":\"from Me\"},{\"word\":\"śṛṇu\",\"translation\":\"just hear\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":4164,\"bb\":3663,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/16/6/b3663/\",\"body_value\":\"O son of Pṛthā, in this world there are two kinds of created beings. One is called divine and the other demoniac. I have already explained to you at length the divine qualities. Now hear from Me of the demoniac.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":4165,\"bb\":3664,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/16/6/b3664/\",\"body_value\":\"Lord Kṛṣṇa, having assured Arjuna that he was born with the divine qualities, is now describing the demoniac way. The conditioned living entities are divided into two classes in this world. Those who are born with divine qualities follow a regulated life; that is to say they abide by the injunctions in scriptures and by the authorities. One should perform duties in the light of authoritative scripture. This mentality is called divine. One who does not follow the regulative principles as they are laid down in the scriptures and who acts according to his whims is called demoniac or asuric. There is no other criterion but obedience to the regulative principles of scriptures. It is mentioned in Vedic literature that both the demigods and the demons are born of the Prajāpati; the only difference is that one class obeys the Vedic injunctions and the other does not.\"}]}],\"short_title\":\"Bg. 16.6\",\"medium_title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is 16.6\"},\"locale\":\"en\",\"activeView\":\"$6:props:activeView\"}]}],\"$L25\",\"$L26\",\"$L27\"]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"29:I[83068,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n2f:I[78455,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n25:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-4 w-full max-w-screen-xl mx-auto md:px-8 mb-3\",\"chil